From db564dfa255e165899adfb415e7f720cad4aa8fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iimmyy <i.a.martins001@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 08:29:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 46/48] mtmd gemma4a: log(mel + 0.001) like Gemma 4's feature
 extractor (log(max(mel, 0.001)) put 8% of a hi-hat's values off by more than
 0.05, up to 0.54; now within 0.0007 of transformers), and wider ears: with
 clip.audio.wide_bands the sound comes at 48 kHz, the 128 bands come from its
 16 kHz version (scipy resample_poly(x, 1, 3)'s 61-tap Kaiser filter), the
 bands above 8 kHz from the 48 kHz sound itself (20 ms Hann frames in a
 1024-point FFT, measured from the floor), and a side path (a.wide.conv1d.*,
 a.wide.proj) adds its projection to the input projection. Front end within
 0.0014 of the PyTorch reference (LittleGuy tools/ears/widen.py).

---
 tools/mtmd/clip-impl.h        |   4 +
 tools/mtmd/clip-model.h       |   5 ++
 tools/mtmd/clip.cpp           |  14 ++++
 tools/mtmd/models/gemma4a.cpp |  44 +++++++----
 tools/mtmd/mtmd-audio.cpp     | 134 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 tools/mtmd/mtmd-audio.h       |   4 +
 6 files changed, 186 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

